PATCH 191: thread the DROPPED nested-paint args of FUN_0000_584a's `[DGROUP:0x6c8]=294d` call (asm 0x587f).

584a (patch 181, the 209e-dispatched viewport paint node) ends `push ax; lea bx,[bx+4]; mov al,0; call
[0x61a]; pop ax; inc [bx]; inc [bx+2]; call [0x6c8]; dec [bx]; dec [bx+2]`.  The nested method
`call [0x6c8]` = MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_294d (the transparency sprite-blit dispatcher, patch 136) is reached
with ax = the POPPED unmasked value (the sprite-directory byte offset = 294d param_1) and bx = node+4
(the position descriptor = 294d param_4).  Patch 181 emitted the far-vector call with NO args, so 294d
-> 298a blitted a GARBAGE sprite (runaway width/height from an unloaded header) -> the flaky
127/128-class SIGSEGV in m_mga_FUN_0000_298a (the documented "298a runaway due to uninitialised
geometry").  Thread ax (unmasked, saved before the al=0 mask) and bx into the c6c8 call per 294d's
__allregs contract (param_1=ax sprite-dir, param_4=bx position).

OBSERVED: with the args threaded, 294d/298a blit a sane sprite -> the paint walk 459a completes
crash-free -> the mission-screen 22dd interpreter now RUNS and advances past 2322 to dispatch the next
handler (0x23ea).  5/5 cascade repros crash-free (was flaky ~50% SIGSEGV).  Reached only on the ACCEPT
cascade -> behaviour-neutral for the 19 flows.  Sources stay pristine; fist.c via build/.

